1. e4 e5 2. f4 exf4 3. Nf3 g5 4. h4 f6 $4 {Diagram #} (4... g4 {is forced: k's idea of supporting the pawn-chain is positionally well-motivated, but...}) 5. Nxg5 $1 fxg5 6. Qh5+ Ke7 7. Qxg5+ Ke8 $2 (7... Nf6 8. e5 Kf7 9. exf6 Qxf6 10. Bc4+ Ke7 11. d4 {will leave white with an extra pawn and a clear advantage, but the text goes down without a fight.}) 8. Qh5+ $1 (8. Qe5+ $6 Qe7 9. Qxh8 Qxe4+ {gives black counterplay of sorts.}) 8... Ke7 9. Qe5+ Kf7 10. Bc4+ Kg6 11. Qf5+ (11. h5+ {is mate in four:} Kh6 12. Qxf4+ Kg7 (12... Qg5 13. Qxf8+ Qg7 14. d3#) 13. h6+ Nxh6 14. Qxh6#) 11... Kg7 12. Qf7+ Kh6 13. Qxf4+ (13. d4 Qf6 14. Bxf4+ {1-0 Gorecki,J-Bojanowski,P/Barlinek 2001}) 13... Kg7 14. Qf7+ Kh6 15. d3+ 1-0

